body:
I believe I found the relevant code. In `render_scene_cull.cpp` starting at line 2690:

```cpp
if (view_count == 1) {
	camera_data.set_camera(transforms[0], projections[0], false, false, camera->vaspect, jitter, p_jitter_phase_count, camera->visible_layers);
} else if (view_count == 2) {
	camera_data.set_multiview_camera(view_count, transforms, projections, false, false, camera->vaspect);
} else {
	// this won't be called (see fail check above) but keeping this comment to indicate we may support more then 2 views in the future...
}
```

`camera->visible_layers` is not passed to `RendererSceneRender::CameraData::set_multiview_camera` when a camera with two views is rendering. And as suspected, `set_multiview_camera` always sets the visible layers to all layers:

```cpp
visible_layers = 0xFFFFFFFF;
```

I don't see any reason not to pass the camera layers to `set_multiview_camera` and set them accordingly, just like the normal `set_camera` does. Am I missing something? If not, I can test and open a PR.

Edit: that does fix the issue, I opened a PR with the change.
